iculty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1b674b8-42f0-554a-a8bb-dca66da0c226" :question/math-academy-id "q-98017" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4x}-1?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $y=\\frac{1}{4x}-1,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/a3/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4x}.$\n\n![](images/02/027b68fffd1555cc1735fc53a634684b019d396fd48bf7df9d430377ba56df21.png)\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units down to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{4x}-1.$\n\n![](images/e1/e1777e170fe23faa53a53a743ef9a6135451b2ed1b11762b146627790a6aacf8.png)"}]}
